SPEC = {'file': 'cover_muzz_junior_product_data_analyst', 'label': 'Muzz Junior Product Data Analyst', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Junior Product Data Analyst position at Muzz in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is close to what I do every day: defining the metrics that matter, building the dashboards people use to track them, and testing whether a change actually made things better.', 'What attracts me most to Muzz is that small improvements to a user journey matter to a very large community across many markets, and that the role sits between product and commercial decisions. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved, and a fast-moving data team close to the product is where I work best.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked. I present the findings to cross-functional stakeholders, so I am used to explaining what the data means to people who need to act on it.', "Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I designed the evaluation framework for a client's AI product, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether a knowledge graph actually improved output quality. I also turned more than 4,800 unstructured patient consultation threads into structured data with a regex and LLM extraction pipeline.", 'On experimentation and statistics, my MSc gave me a strong grounding in hypothesis testing, experimental design and causal inference. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application so that people can run scenarios without touching the code. Explaining results clearly to people who do not want the method is something I have done at Ipsos Strategy3 and with pharmaceutical client stakeholders.', 'Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my SQL, dashboard and experimentation experience could contribute to the Muzz data team.']}
